_model: docspage
---
title: Enable a repository
---
menu: /help/docs/vcs
---
sort_key: 1
---
body:

This guide will walk you through the steps to enable a GitHub repository or GitLab project for integration, ensuring it is properly linked. Once connected, new releases from the repository will be automatically ingested and archived.

As a prerequisite, make sure you have a connected GitHub or GitLab account. Learn here how to connect your account here:

- [Linking your GitHub/GitLab/ORCID/OpenAIRE account](https://help.zenodo.org/docs/profile/linking-accounts/)

---
docs:

#### docsheader ####

text: Enable a GitHub repository
----
ref:enable-a-github-repository
#### docsstep ####
step: 1
----
text: Click the profile menu in the header and click **GitHub**
----
image: profile.png
----
#### docsstep ####
step: 2
----
text: Click **Sync now** in the header
----
image: sync.png
----
#### docsstep ####
step: 3
----
text: Find a repository you wish to enable, then toggle the slider to connect it to Zenodo
----
image: repos.png
----
#### docsstep ####
step: 4
----
text: The repository is now connected to Zenodo:
----
image: success_repo.png
----
#### docsstep ####
step: 5
----
text: Refresh the page to update the list of enabled repositories
----
image: enabled_repos.png
----
#### docsheader ####

text: Enable a GitLab project
----
ref:enable-a-github-repository
#### docsstep ####
step: 1
----
text: Click the profile menu in the header and click **GitLab**
----
image: profile_gitlab.png
----
#### docsstep ####
step: 2
----
text: Click **Sync now** in the header
----
image: sync_gitlab.png
----
#### docsstep ####
step: 3
----
text: Find a project you wish to enable, then toggle the slider to connect it to Zenodo
----
image: projects.png
----
#### docsstep ####
step: 4
----
text: The project is now connected to Zenodo:
----
image: success_project.png
----
#### docsstep ####
step: 5
----
text: Refresh the page to update the list of enabled projects
----
image: enabled_projects.png
